# Sothëkavath, the Compounded Soldier — swamp T3 legendary tank

[title Sothëkavath, the Compounded Soldier]
[image monsters/swamp_boss.png]
[blood #3a3024]
[stats hp=28]

* move Heavy Defend
  narration: Sothëkavath sets the thousand-year guard. Steel from a dozen eras hardens at once.

* move Heavy Attack
  narration: The blade moves in a hand that has held a blade longer than any one hand should.
  narration: A thousand soldiers swing it in a single hand, and the blade comes around clean.

* move Defend
  narration: It turns its mass a fraction sideways. The seams in its skin pull tighter.

* move Recover
  narration: The voices inside it argue, agree, and the worn places re-knit themselves between layers.

* move Brutal Heavy Slow Stunning Attack
  narration: All of the soldiers in it commit to the strike together, and you eat all of it together.

* move Heavy Slow Recover
  narration: Every layer settles back into place at once — the seams close, the blood re-routes, and a thousand years of standing here standing back up reasserts itself.

* intro
The clearing was a battle once and is again. The thing in the middle of
it is the size of two men and built from more — armor from a dozen eras
layered into the skin, the seams of it healed and reopened a thousand
times. It turns toward you, and its mouth moves, and many voices come
out at once — all of them angry, none of them at you, all of them
speaking your name. Not the name on your papers. The name your
grandmother carried. It plants its feet in the mud where it has planted
its feet for a thousand years, and it lifts the blade.

* win
+gold 25
+tag killed_sothekavath
The seams in the layered armor open one last time and do not close. The
voices come out of the mouth in twos and threes and finally singly, and
finally none. The mud where it has planted its feet for a thousand
years takes it back. The clearing was a battle and is, again, just a
clearing.

* lose
The voices speak your name in twos and threes and finally singly, and
finally none. The clearing was a battle, and is, again.
